    "summary": "Cloth (woman’s wrapper), formed of twenty narrow strips of imported industrial cotton, hand-woven and hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The strips are of two types, arranged alternately. One has no pattern, and is of uniform pink thread in both warp and weft. The other is of uniform green thread in both warp and weft with a central warp band of yellow, and is embellished with a regularly repeating pattern created by using bundles of supplementary yellow thread. The cloth has not been hemmed.",
